==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gmw-pro|gem-pro|inh=2}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|schif}}, from {{inh|de|goh|skif|t=ship, barrel, vessel}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*skip}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*skipą|t=ship, hollow object}}. The sense {{m-g|nave}} is a {{semantic loan|de|la|nāvis|nocap=1}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nds|Schipp}}, {{cog|fy|skip}}, {{cog|nl|schip}}, {{cog|yi|שיף}}, {{cog|en|ship}}, {{cog|da|skib}}, {{cog|sv|skepp}}. Related also to Lithuanian {{m|lt|skiẽbti||to rip up}}, Latvian {{m|lv|skibit|škibît|to cut, lop}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ʃɪf/}}
* {{rhymes|de|ɪf|s=1}}
* {{audio|de|De-Schiff.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-Schiff.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

